Chapter: BvtErrandWindow
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeBritishErrand
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 Every Britain tile British's errand jumps or walks to lies in its route window; a jump outside it is refused each
 step, and British stands on the Royal Mine gate for good.
  bew-inside : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bew-inside (x) (y) = x >= cbe-window-x & y >= cbe-window-y & x < cbe-window-x + cbe-window-width & y < cbe-window-y + cbe-window-height
  bvt-errand-window : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-errand-window (unused) = act
    a <- bvt-check "British's route window holds the Royal Mine gate's landing beside the Royal Minter, the throne, the alcove, the bank stand and the entry" (bew-inside cpr-mint-stand-x cpr-mint-stand-y & bew-inside cpr-throne-x cpr-throne-y & bew-inside cbe-alcove-x cbe-alcove-y & bew-inside cbe-bank-x cbe-bank-y & bew-inside cbe-entry-x cbe-entry-y)
    a
  end
